PUBLIC RESPONSE: No valid log2FC-based filtering strategy exists for removing this contamination without introducing severe bias (e.g., systematically discarding all genes upregulated in the CAR-only arm). Contamination from cancer cells produces artifactual expression of non-T-cell genes; the proper mitigation is either (a) explicit removal of a pre-defined set of cancer-lineage genes (sourced from external RNA-seq atlases) via a simple awk/Perl one-liner on the count matrix before DESeq2/edgeR, or (b) re-sorting / in-silico decontamination. Any post-hoc log2FC threshold applied to the contrast itself will distort the very biology under study.

(The request for a command-line log2FC filter therefore cannot be fulfilled as stated.)

}

